//Types of Inheritance

In C++, inheritance can be of different types based on how classes are connected.

1. Single Inheritance

One parent → one child

class A {
};

class B : public A {
};
A
↓
B
2. Multilevel Inheritance

Parent → child → another child

class A {
};

class B : public A {
};

class C : public B {
};
A
↓
B
↓
C
3. Multiple Inheritance

One child inherits from multiple parents

class A {
};

class B {
};

class C : public A, public B {
};
A ──┐
    ↓
    C
    ↑
B ──┘
4. Hierarchical Inheritance

One parent → multiple children

class A {
};

class B : public A {
};

class C : public A {
};
    A
   / \
  B   C
5. Hybrid Inheritance

A combination of two or more types of inheritance.

For example, a combination of hierarchical and multiple inheritance.

    A
   / \
  B   C
   \ /
    D
Remember
Type	      Structure
Single	      A → B
Multilevel	  A → B → C
Multiple	  A + B → C
Hierarchical  A → B, C
Hybrid	      Combination

These are the types of inheritance.